# NextFinUp production crontab — source of truth for the server's cron jobs.
#
# The live crontab on the server can drift from this file if someone edits it directly with
# `crontab -e`. After changing this file, apply it on the server with:
#   crontab deploy/crontab
# and after editing on the server, sync it back here with:
#   crontab -l > deploy/crontab
#
# Read-only view of whatever is currently live: /admin-tools/cron/ (articles.views.cron_status_view).
#
# Every job runs through deploy/run_job.sh, which (1) prefixes each output line with a timestamp
# before appending to the log file — plain `>>` gives no way to tell when a line was written,
# which makes correlating failures across jobs hard during an incident — and (2) emails
# settings.ADMINS via the notify_failure command if the job exits non-zero (eg. OOM kill), so a
# quiet cron failure doesn't go unnoticed until someone happens to read the log.
#
# TIMEZONE: this server's system clock and Django's TIME_ZONE are both UTC, and cron itself has
# no per-job TZ override — so every "hour" below is UTC, NOT Korea time (KST = UTC+9). All times
# are chosen so the KST wall-clock time next to each line is what actually happens; get the KST
# figure by adding 9 hours (and rolling the date forward past 24:00).

*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/nextfinup && deploy/run_job.sh logs/collect_keyword_news.log venv/bin/python manage.py collect_keyword_news
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/nextfinup && deploy/run_job.sh logs/collect_market_index.log venv/bin/python manage.py collect_market_index
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/nextfinup && deploy/run_job.sh logs/collect_kis_news.log venv/bin/python manage.py collect_kis_news
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/nextfinup && deploy/run_job.sh logs/collect_stock_realtime_price.log venv/bin/python manage.py collect_stock_realtime_price
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/nextfinup && deploy/run_job.sh logs/collect_fluctuation_ranking.log venv/bin/python manage.py collect_fluctuation_ranking
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/nextfinup && deploy/run_job.sh logs/collect_global_market_data.log venv/bin/python manage.py collect_global_market_data
